{"name":"Tree Swing","hex":"#726144","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tree","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial woody plant taller and larger than a shrub with a wooden trunk and, at some distance from the ground, having leaves and branches.","Any other plant (such as a large shrub or herb) that is reminiscent of the above in form and size."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To chase (an animal or person) up a tree.","To place in a tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree"},{"term":"swing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To rotate about an off-centre fixed point.","To dance."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act, or an instance, of swinging.","The manner in which something is swung."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Swing (seat)","blocks":[{"text":"A swing is a seat or platform, suspended from chains, ropes, or bars, on which one or more people can swing back and forth for enjoyment or relaxation. Swings are a common piece of equipment at children's playgrounds and may also be found in yards or gardens, on porches, inside homes, or as freestanding public play equipment like the Estonian village swing. Swings have a long history in many different parts of the world and come in various types."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/MoSchaukel.jpg/330px-MoSchaukel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swing_(seat)"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"htt